# PhantasmHothouse Rules

This is a Cleveland Music Co. Hothouse / Daisy Seed firmware project.

The project is intentionally GPL.

Main working folder:
src/PhantasmHothouse

Hard rules:
- Do not edit files outside src/PhantasmHothouse unless explicitly asked.
- Do not modify libDaisy.
- Do not modify DaisySP.
- Do not modify other Hothouse example projects.
- Do not touch src/buzzbox_octa_squawker.
- Always inspect before editing.
- Make small incremental changes.
- After every code change, build with:
  make -C src/PhantasmHothouse clean
  make -C src/PhantasmHothouse
- If the build fails, stop and show the exact error.
- Do not continue adding features on top of a broken build.
- Keep the code readable and suitable for embedded real-time audio.
- Avoid heap allocation in the audio callback.
- Avoid expensive unnecessary work in the per-sample loop.
- Use smoothing for parameters that can click.
- Use SDRAM for large delay/freeze buffers.
- Keep the dry path clean and preserve amp feel.

Project identity:
- This is not an Echoplex or tape-delay clone.
- Do not copy the Echoplex DSP identity from the Hothouse examples.
- The pedal is a Phantasmagoria-inspired reverse/freeze delay for Hothouse.
- Keep my own delay, reverse, and freeze identity separate.

Milestones:
v0.1 Clean Hardware Skeleton
v0.2 Basic Delay
v0.3 Reverse Delay
v0.4 Freeze
v0.5 Accumulate / Performance Behavior
v1.0 Release
